  "_comment_source": "GENERATED FROM THE BOM. Every name, price, buyback and quantity below is copied from docs/gameplan/data/materials.json, which is itself generated from docs/gameplan/02-BOM/master-materials-and-mint.md. If a number here disagrees with that file, that file wins - fix it here, do not fix it there. The item_id values are the BOM's own ids, so the two can always be diffed line for line.",

  "_comment_currency": "Kasu. Denominations 10 / 20 / 50 / 100 / 500 - coin CAD lives in openmarket/. round_to is 10 because that is the smallest coin: every displayed price must be payable with coins that physically exist.",
  "currency": "Kasu",
  "currency_symbol": "",
  "round_to": 10,

  "_comment_math": "COMPOUNDING, NOT ADDITIVE. Each fired event multiplies the CURRENT price and the result is rounded UP to the nearest 10 before the next event is applied:  war  price = ceil10(base x 1.2),  then tariff  price = ceil10(war x 1.3). Cumulative effect is x1.56, not x1.50. This reproduces the war/tariff columns in the BOM exactly - see server/market.py.",

  "_comment_buyback": "Buyback is ALWAYS against the base price, never the live price. Without that, teams arbitrage the price shocks by buying early and selling into war pricing. fresh = unused and in original condition; modified = cut but still usable. Unusable material is bought back at nothing. Every base price is a multiple of 20, so modified is always payable in coins.",

  "_comment_stock": "basekit = pieces already distributed across the ten team boxes. depot = pieces on the depot shelf. procure = the two added up, i.e. what was actually bought. Shown on the admin panel only - the depot board deliberately does not display stock, because a visible count invites teams to race each other for the last one.",

